From 95d440e318091bcdba3d4ffbaa2fe33a22b821f8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Bourgoin <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
Date: Mon, 30 Mar 2026 11:41:49 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 251/913] core: scmi-server: dump source files from
 SCP-firmware v2.16.0

Dump the source tree of SCP-firmware from its release tag v2.16.0.
URL: https://git.gitlab.arm.com/firmware/SCP-firmware.git
Tag: f76402dfefc7 ("doc: Notice on update on SCP contribution policy")

Not all the file from SCP-firmware source are dumped into OP-TEE OS
unitary tests framework are left aside.

Update scripts/checkpatch_inc.sh to not run checkpatch tool on
SCP-firmware source tree changes since SCP-firmware coding style
differs from OP-TEE coding style. Instead, one should use the Python
scripts from SCP-firmware/tools/.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [ST downstream https://github.com/STMicroelectronics/optee_os.git 1347eb8de4eaf2c938acf363472b482b6ead0a45 core: scmi-server: dump source files from SCP-firmware v2.16.0]
Change-Id: I66b7c85ba2b0fd41dc76b6dd5a60ed7df394abac
Signed-off-by: Thomas Bourgoin <thomas.bourgoin@foss.st.com>
